+# 008: The board and the card
+
+A new pattern, and a case added to D3. No component, theme, receipt or lint change: the board and the card compose existing crease components with values the receipt already allows.
+
+## Why
+
+Each team's page needed a board: one column per status, each issue a card. `patterns.md` named a board as a new pattern to decide first, and `IssueRow` left the card undecided.
+
+## What changed
+
+- `src/design/issue-card.ts`: `IssueCard`. An `item` with the `outline` look and the `sm` size. The parts and their order are the row's (D3): priority, identifier and status; the title; labels, date and assignee. The title wraps, because a column is narrow. Priority, status and assignee are PropertyPickers (D7); changing the status moves the card to its new column, which is the pointer route between columns (D9). There is no drag and drop.
+- `src/design/issue-board.ts`: `IssueBoard`. One column per status in workflow order (`STATUSES_IN_ORDER`), empty columns included. The column header is the group header without the collapse button. Columns are 272px and never shrink; the board scrolls sideways.
+- `src/design/issue-collection.ts`: a fourth body, `board`, so the board shares the controls bar with the list.
+- `src/design/app-sidebar.ts`: the rules name Board as a team's second page, without a count.
+- `design-system/principles.md`: D3 gains the card case.
+- `design-system/patterns.md`: `IssueBoard` and `IssueCard`.
+- Feature: the views `board:eng` and `board:des`, a Board link under each team, a "Layout" switch on a team's page, and Go to entries in the command menu.
+
+## Open
+
+- The browser check does not cover the board yet: cards at 900px and on a phone, sideways scrolling, and focus return from a card's picker.
+- Grouping and collapsed groups do not apply to a board; the "Grouped by status" control is hidden there.
